course: dictionary
lesson: 10267
title: Everyday words: toothbrush
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A toothbrush is a small brush with a long handle. You use it with toothpaste to clean your teeth. The name tells you the job: a brush for teeth.
explain: Read the sentence for clues. «Each person uses only their own toothbrush, because sharing spreads germs.» The reason after "because" tells you why a toothbrush belongs to one person only.
explain: Health lessons teach a routine: brush your teeth twice a day for about two minutes, with a soft toothbrush and fluoride toothpaste. Get a new toothbrush every three months, or sooner when the bristles are splayed (spread out and bent).
fact: A toothbrush is a small brush with a long handle, used with toothpaste to clean your teeth.
fact: Brush your teeth twice a day for about two minutes.
fact: Do not share a toothbrush, because germs spread.
fact: «Electric toothbrush» means a toothbrush that is powered, so it moves for you.
fact: A toothbrush cannot reach the narrow gaps between teeth, so clean those with floss or a small brush made for gaps, once a day.
exercise: «Each person uses only their own toothbrush, because sharing spreads germs.» Why should you not share a toothbrush? | Because toothpaste is expensive | *Because germs spread | Because it is too long | Because it makes hair grow
exercise: What do you use a toothbrush with, to clean your teeth? | *Toothpaste | Soap for your hands | Shampoo for your hair
exercise: «A toothbrush cleans the fronts, backs and tops of the teeth, but it cannot reach the narrow gaps between them.» What cleans those gaps? | Water from the tap | Only a bigger toothbrush | Nothing, gaps do not need cleaning | *Floss or a small brush made for the gaps
test: How long should you brush your teeth for? | About an hour | *About two minutes | About two seconds | About twenty minutes
test: What does «toothbrush holder» mean? | A bathroom light | A brush for cleaning hair | A small cup of toothpaste | *A place where you keep your toothbrush
exam: Mum says, «Put toothpaste on your toothbrush, then brush for two minutes.» What do you put the toothpaste on? | Your shoes | The bath | Your hair | *Your toothbrush
